IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`
IMPORT `je54-seat`
IMPORT `je54-seat-powers-and-penalties`

-- je54-tests-independent: an independent test author's answers to scenarios on the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 (L.17/1954).
--
-- STATUS: every expected value in this file is "assumed, not ruled".
-- It is one reader's reading of the deposited texts.  Nobody with authority has ruled on any reading.
-- Most expected values were decided from the seven texts of the Law (and, for commencement around 28 September 2021 only,
-- Articles 3(2) and 3(6) of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021) BEFORE the encoding was opened, and were written down in
-- decisions.md in the author's scratch directory; their IDs (A01, E03, ...) are the IDs of that file.  CORRECTED AFTER THE RUN: a few dozen scenarios (every ID with a letter suffix, such as N10b or P13b, and some others) were added while this file was being written, AFTER the exported names and the "some other ..." options had been read, and are not in decisions.md; the O09 below is not the O09 of decisions.md.
-- The encoding's exported names were read afterwards, to learn how to call them; no expected value was changed after a run, and the only change to this file after the run is this comment and the O09 label.
-- SPLIT.  Part 2 of 3 of the independent test pass, cut by Article after the run so that no file passes about 600 lines: Article 7 (service by post), Article 8 (bankruptcy), Articles 12 to 15, the dates before 1 January 2019 and the unsure scenarios (sections S and U sit here because they reuse the local definitions of K, L and O); sections K, L, O, S, U.
-- The header and the Helpers section are repeated in each part.  No assertion was altered, deleted or moved to another section; the 520 assertions of the original are the 520 across the three parts.
--
-- VERSIONS.  V1 = l_17_1954_20210927 (1 Jan 2019 to 27 Sep 2021); V2a = l_17_1954_20220130 (28 Sep 2021 to 30 Jan 2022);
-- V2b = l_17_1954_20220831 (31 Jan to 31 Aug 2022); V2c = l_17_1954_20240110 (1 Sep 2022 to 10 Jan 2024);
-- V2d = l_17_1954_20251123 (11 Jan 2024 to 23 Nov 2025); V2e = l_17_1954_20260618 (24 Nov 2025 to 18 Jun 2026);
-- V2f = l_17_1954.current (19 Jun 2026 to current).  "V1 src:9" means line 9 of the V1 text, and so on for each version.
--
-- CLOSED OR SILENT.  Where the Law gives a closed answer a negative is FALSE.  Where the Law is silent the answer is a refusal.
-- Where an Article carries "unless the contrary intention appears" (or the context, or, in Article 11A, "the contrary is expressed")
-- and the input says it does appear, the Law says only that its own construction does not apply, never what applies instead:
-- the answer is a refusal, not FALSE.  Where an Article carries no such qualifier (13(2), for one) the input has no effect.
-- The text of a refusal is not asserted except for dates before 1 January 2019, whose message the brief fixes.
--
-- COMMENCEMENT.  An enactment "expressed to come into operation on a particular day" comes into operation "immediately on the
-- expiration of the previous day" (V1 Art 1(5), V1 src:9), that is at the start of that day.  One that is silent or says forthwith
-- is construed as expressed to come into operation on the day it was passed or made (V1 Art 1(6), V1 src:10), so, read together,
-- at the start of that day, even though that is before it was made.  The moment asserted is the start of the day on the clock of
-- the zone named (Etc/UTC unless said); the Law names no zone.

§ `Helpers`

GIVEN how IS A `How an enactment expresses the time of its commencement`
      named IS A MAYBE DATE
      made IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`stated as` how named made MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS how
        `the day it names` IS named
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS NOTHING

GIVEN how IS A `How an enactment expresses the time of its commencement`
      named IS A MAYBE DATE
      made IS A DATE
      asked IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Commencement as stated`
`stated as and asked on` how named made asked MEANS
    `Commencement as stated` WITH
        `how it is expressed` IS how
        `the day it names` IS named
        `the day it was passed or made` IS made
        `the day the question is asked` IS JUST asked

`reading by commencement` MEANS `whether the enactment had come into force before 28 September 2021`
`reading by day made` MEANS `the day the enactment was passed or made`
`reading by day asked` MEANS `the day on which the question about the enactment is asked`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, mo IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATETIME
`UTC moment` y mo d h mi s MEANS DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (YMD y mo d) (TIME_FROM_HMS h mi s) "Etc/UTC"

GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      r IS A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
GIVETH A DATE
`day of commencement` c r MEANS (`on what day did the enactment come into force` c r)'s `the day`

GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      r IS A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
GIVETH A `Basis of a reading`
`basis of commencement` c r MEANS (`on what day did the enactment come into force` c r)'s `the basis`

GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      zone IS A STRING
      r IS A `Which day selects the text for commencement`
GIVETH A DATETIME
`moment of commencement` c zone r MEANS (`at what moment did the enactment come into force` c zone r)'s `the moment`

GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      y IS A NUMBER, mo IS A NUMBER, d IS A NUMBER, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`in force at the UTC moment` c y mo d h mi s MEANS
    (`was the enactment in force at a moment` (`UTC moment` y mo d h mi s) "Etc/UTC" c `reading by commencement`)'s `the answer`

GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`in force on the day` c d MEANS
    (`was the enactment in force on a day` d c `reading by commencement`)'s `the answer`

GIVEN d IS A DATE, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Local moment`
`local moment` d h mi s MEANS
    `Local moment` WITH
        `calendar day` IS d
        `hour of the day` IS h
        `minute of the hour` IS mi
        `second of the minute` IS s

GIVEN m IS A `Local moment`
      d IS A DATE, h IS A NUMBER, mi IS A NUMBER, s IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the local moment is` m d h mi s MEANS
    m's `calendar day` EQUALS d AND m's `hour of the day` EQUALS h AND m's `minute of the hour` EQUALS mi AND m's `second of the minute` EQUALS s

§ `K. Article 7: service by post (the same text in all seven versions)`

GIVEN auth IS A BOOLEAN
      addressed IS A BOOLEAN
      prepaid IS A BOOLEAN
      posted IS A BOOLEAN
      ordinary IS A `Local moment`
      other IS A MAYBE `Local moment`
GIVETH A `Service by post as it happened`
`letter` auth addressed prepaid posted ordinary other MEANS
    `Service by post as it happened` WITH
        `the enactment authorizes or requires the document to be served by post` IS auth
        `the letter was properly addressed` IS addressed
        `the letter was prepaid` IS prepaid
        `the letter was posted` IS posted
        `the time at which the letter would be delivered in the ordinary course of post` IS ordinary
        `the other time proved` IS other

`the usual letter` MEANS `letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0) NOTHING

-- K01  V1 src:30: posted Mon 2020-06-01, properly addressed, prepaid and posted; ordinary-course delivery Wed 2020-06-03 11:00: deemed effected at that time, not at the posting
#ASSERT `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) `the usual letter` FALSE
#ASSERT `the local moment is` (`at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) `the usual letter` FALSE `the time that is proved`) (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0
#ASSERT `on what day is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) `the usual letter` FALSE `the time that is proved` EQUALS YMD 2020 6 3
-- K04  V1 src:30: the letter was not properly addressed: no deeming by Article 7, and no time
#ASSERT `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`letter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0) NOTHING) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`letter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0) NOTHING) FALSE `the time that is proved`
-- K05  postage not prepaid
#ASSERT `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`letter` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0) NOTHING) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- K05b  the letter was not posted
#ASSERT `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0) NOTHING) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- K06-K07  the enactment does not authorize or require service by post: Article 7 deals only with that case, and says nothing about the rest
#ASSERT REFUSED `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`letter` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0) NOTHING) FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`letter` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0) NOTHING) FALSE `the time that is proved`
-- K10  V1 src:30 "unless the contrary intention appears"
#ASSERT REFUSED `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) `the usual letter` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) `the usual letter` TRUE `the time that is proved`
-- K11  V1 src:30 with the Schedule "midnight" V1 src:107: a notice to be served by midnight on 2020-06-03; deemed effected 2020-06-03 11:00: in time
#ASSERT (`was the thing done by midnight on the day` (YMD 2020 6 3) (`at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) `the usual letter` FALSE `the time that is proved`))'s `the answer`
-- K12  deemed effected 2020-06-04 00:00:00: after the midnight of 2020-06-03
#ASSERT (`was the thing done by midnight on the day` (YMD 2020 6 3) (`at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 4) 0 0 0) NOTHING) FALSE `the time that is proved`))'s `the answer` EQUALS FALSE
-- K13  deemed effected 2020-06-03 23:59:59: the last second of the day, in time
#ASSERT (`was the thing done by midnight on the day` (YMD 2020 6 3) (`at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 3) 23 59 59) NOTHING) FALSE `the time that is proved`))'s `the answer`
-- K14  posted 2018-06-01 (Article 7 was Article 12 before renumbering; no text deposited)
#ASSERT REFUSED `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2018 6 1) `the usual letter` FALSE
    BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"
#ASSERT REFUSED `at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2018 6 1) `the usual letter` FALSE `the time that is proved`
-- K15  V2f src:27: posted 2026-10-01, the same facts, the same answer
#ASSERT `the local moment is` (`at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2026 10 1) `the usual letter` FALSE `the time that is proved`) (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0
-- K16  last day of V1 and first day of V2a: no change at the boundary
#ASSERT `the local moment is` (`at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2021 9 27) `the usual letter` FALSE `the time that is proved`) (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0
#ASSERT `the local moment is` (`at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2021 9 28) `the usual letter` FALSE `the time that is proved`) (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0
-- K16b  the other four versions
#ASSERT `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2022 3 1) `the usual letter` FALSE
#ASSERT `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2023 3 1) `the usual letter` FALSE
#ASSERT `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2025 3 1) `the usual letter` FALSE
#ASSERT `is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2026 3 1) `the usual letter` FALSE

§ `L. Article 8: a person becoming bankrupt (event date selects the text)`

`event remise` MEANS `the Royal Court grants the person's own application to place the person's property under the control of the Court`
`event desastre` MEANS `the person's property is declared en désastre`
`event Viscount` MEANS `the Viscount grants a debt remission order in respect of the person's qualifying debts under the Debt Remission (Individuals) (Jersey) Law 2016`
`event cession` MEANS `the Royal Court grants the person's own application to make a general cession of the person's property`
`event renounced` MEANS `the Royal Court adjudges the person's property to be renounced`
`event company creditors` MEANS `a company is wound up by means of a creditors' winding up pursuant to the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
`event administration` MEANS `an administration order is made in respect of a company under Part 20B of the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991`
`event LLC` MEANS `a limited liability company is wound up by means of a creditors' winding up under the Limited Liability Companies (Winding Up and Dissolution) (Jersey) Regulations 2022`
`event bank` MEANS `a bank winding up order is made under the Bank (Recovery and Resolution) (Jersey) Law 2017`
`event other` MEANS `some other event`

`person individual` MEANS `Person who may have become bankrupt` WITH
    `is a company` IS FALSE
    `is a limited liability company` IS FALSE
    `is a bank` IS FALSE
`person company` MEANS `Person who may have become bankrupt` WITH
    `is a company` IS TRUE
    `is a limited liability company` IS FALSE
    `is a bank` IS FALSE
`person llc` MEANS `Person who may have become bankrupt` WITH
    `is a company` IS FALSE
    `is a limited liability company` IS TRUE
    `is a bank` IS FALSE
`person bank` MEANS `Person who may have become bankrupt` WITH
    `is a company` IS FALSE
    `is a limited liability company` IS FALSE
    `is a bank` IS TRUE

GIVEN e IS AN `Event in the life of a person`
      p IS A `Person who may have become bankrupt`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`bankrupt by the text of the day of the event` e p d MEANS
    `is the event a person becoming bankrupt` e p d d FALSE `the day of the event`

-- L01  V1 src:33 (a): the Royal Court grants the person's own application to place the person's property under its control
#ASSERT `bankrupt by the text of the day of the event` `event remise` `person individual` (YMD 2020 3 10)
-- L02  V1 src:34 (b): the property is declared en désastre
#ASSERT `bankrupt by the text of the day of the event` `event desastre` `person individual` (YMD 2020 3 10)
-- L03  V1 src:35 (ba): the Viscount grants a debt remission order
#ASSERT `bankrupt by the text of the day of the event` `event Viscount` `person individual` (YMD 2020 3 10)
-- L04  V1 src:36 (c): the Royal Court grants the person's own application for a general cession
#ASSERT `bankrupt by the text of the day of the event` `event cession` `person individual` (YMD 2020 3 10)
-- L05  V1 src:37 (d): the Royal Court adjudges the property renounced
#ASSERT `bankrupt by the text of the day of the event` `event renounced` `person individual` (YMD 2020 3 10)
-- L06  V1 src:38 (e): a company is wound up by a creditors' winding up under the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991
#ASSERT `bankrupt by the text of the day of the event` `event company creditors` `person company` (YMD 2020 3 10)
-- L07-L09  V1 src:32-38: the list is closed ("construed as references to either"): a members' winding up, a refused application, an application by a creditor are not on it
#ASSERT `bankrupt by the text of the day of the event` `event other` `person company` (YMD 2020 3 10) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `bankrupt by the text of the day of the event` `event other` `person individual` (YMD 2020 3 10) EQUALS FALSE
-- L06b  (e) is "in the case of a company": the event is not a bankruptcy of an individual
#ASSERT `bankrupt by the text of the day of the event` `event company creditors` `person individual` (YMD 2020 3 10) EQUALS FALSE
-- L10  V1: no bank limb (it arrives 31 Jan 2022, V2b src:36)
