§ `U. UNSURE scenarios: where the words allow more than one reading.  Each states the reading taken; the other reading is in the comment.`

-- U02 / E06 / E07  UNSURE.  An enactment naming 28 Sep 2021 (made 27 Sep or 20 Sep): the day is certain.  The governing provision is not:
-- (A) 2021 Law Art 3(6) is not met, because the 2021 Part commences at the same instant (28 Sep 2021) and the enactment did not commence BEFORE it, so 2021 Art 3(2) governs;
-- (B) V1 Art 1(5) still governs.  Only the day is asserted.
#ASSERT `day of commencement` (`stated as` `on a particular day` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 28)) (YMD 2021 9 27)) `reading by commencement` EQUALS YMD 2021 9 28
#ASSERT `day of commencement` (`stated as` `on a particular day` (JUST (YMD 2021 9 28)) (YMD 2021 9 20)) `reading by commencement` EQUALS YMD 2021 9 28

-- U09 / L41  UNSURE.  An LLC creditors' winding up on 2022-06-15, asked on 2025-03-01.  (A) the text in force on the day of the event governs: V2b has no LLC limb, so not a bankruptcy (taken);
-- (B) the text in force on the day of the question governs: V2d has the LLC limb, so a bankruptcy.  No transitional provision is in either text.
#ASSERT `is the event a person becoming bankrupt` `event LLC` `person llc` (YMD 2022 6 15) (YMD 2025 3 1) FALSE `the day of the event` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is the event a person becoming bankrupt` `event LLC` `person llc` (YMD 2022 6 15) (YMD 2025 3 1) FALSE `the day on which the question about the event is asked`
-- U09 / L42  the same for an administration order on 2026-01-10 asked on 2026-10-28
#ASSERT `is the event a person becoming bankrupt` `event administration` `person company` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day of the event` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is the event a person becoming bankrupt` `event administration` `person company` (YMD 2026 1 10) (YMD 2026 10 28) FALSE `the day on which the question about the event is asked`

-- U06 / H12  UNSURE.  Act 1954-08-20 by a body corporate that would not then have been liable.  The proviso says "nothing in this Article"; it does not limit Article 4(1) with the Schedule definition of "person"
-- (V1 src:111: "person" shall include any body of persons corporate or unincorporated).  (A) read literally: by the Schedule only (taken); (B) read purposively: not at all.
#ASSERT `does person include this body` (YMD 2026 10 28) `a body corporate` TRUE FALSE (YMD 1954 8 20) FALSE `the proviso limits Article 3 only` EQUALS `by the Schedule only`

-- U (J04)  UNSURE.  The exact instant at which the substituted provisions come into operation: "remain in force until" the instant they come into operation.  (A) not in force at that instant (taken); (B) still in force at that instant.
#ASSERT `do the repealed provisions remain in force at the instant` (YMD 2020 3 1) TRUE (`UTC moment` 2020 3 1 0 0 0) (JUST (`UTC moment` 2020 3 1 0 0 0)) EQUALS FALSE

-- U14 / D03  UNSURE.  "Where appropriate": not appropriate to read passing as making.  (A) the reference stands as written (taken); (B) the Article gives no reading at all (refusal).
#ASSERT `how is a reference to passing or repeal read` (YMD 2020 6 1) `passing` FALSE EQUALS `as written`

-- U (K03)  UNSURE.  The presumption is rebutted by proof of another time (2020-06-02 09:00): (A) the time proved governs (taken); (B) the Article gives no time (refusal).
#ASSERT `the local moment is` (`at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0) (JUST (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 2) 9 0 0))) FALSE `the time that is proved`) (YMD 2020 6 2) 9 0 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `at what time is service by post deemed effected` (YMD 2020 6 1) (`letter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 3) 11 0 0) (JUST (`local moment` (YMD 2020 6 2) 9 0 0))) FALSE `the Article gives no time`

-- U (E-alt)  The callable alternatives of the commencement fork (the brief's (b) and (c)), by derivation from their definitions.
-- (b) the text in force on the day the enactment was made: made 2021-09-20 naming 2021-10-01, the V1 text governs and gives the same day; made 2021-09-28, silent, the V2a text has no rule.
#ASSERT `day of commencement` (`stated as` `on a particular day` (JUST (YMD 2021 10 1)) (YMD 2021 9 20)) `reading by day made` EQUALS YMD 2021 10 1
#ASSERT `day of commencement` (`stated as` `silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation` NOTHING (YMD 2021 9 27)) `reading by day made` EQUALS YMD 2021 9 27
#ASSERT REFUSED `day of commencement` (`stated as` `silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation` NOTHING (YMD 2021 9 28)) `reading by day made`
-- (c) the text in force on the day the question is asked: asked on 2021-09-27 the V1 text answers; asked on 2026-10-28 the V2f text has no rule.
#ASSERT `day of commencement` (`stated as and asked on` `silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation` NOTHING (YMD 2021 9 27) (YMD 2021 9 27)) `reading by day asked` EQUALS YMD 2021 9 27
#ASSERT REFUSED `day of commencement` (`stated as and asked on` `silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation` NOTHING (YMD 2021 9 27) (YMD 2026 10 28)) `reading by day asked`
